[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi all — new here. Background: I work in ML science and infra, and have an undergrad math degree (real/complex/functional analysis, topology, differential geometry, etc.), but I'm new to Lean and Mathlib and currently working through Mathematics in Lean.</p>\n<p>My longer-term interest is contributing toward Riemannian / differential geometry — I've been reading the recent Mathlib.Geometry.Manifold.Riemannian.* files and would love to eventually help build toward geodesics, the exponential map, and curvature.</p>\n<p>While I'm still ramping, is there a good-first-issue or a small API gap you'd point a newcomer to (geometry or otherwise) to learn the contribution pipeline? Happy to start small and coordinate. Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 598938498,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Korbonits",
        "timestamp": 1780200051
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi Alex, welcome!<br>\nWhile I'm not familiar with Riemannian/differential geometry myself, a general advice for newcomers is to hold off on contributing to Mathlib right away: the bar is quite high, and finding a good first issue can be tricky (though I may be wrong as I don't know the state of this particular area in Mathlib).<br>\nA better starting point is usually to formalize a theorem you already know well. Gaps in the API will naturally surface along the way, and those make for very natural PRs. Don't hesitate to ask for help during the process: it might save you from defining things that already exist under a name you wouldn't have thought to search for.</p>",
        "id": 599007603,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1780245168
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My understanding is that in Riemannian geometry a lot of things are blocked by existing PRs that are still under review; e.g. the Levi-Civita connection which is a prerequisite for curvature is in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36845\">#36845</a>, and there is some ongoing work on geodesics too, though I'm not sure about the current state of that. Maybe e.g. <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"634338\">@Michael Rothgang</span> has more information about that or can recommend you a project though</p>",
        "id": 599009692,
        "sender_full_name": "Ben Eltschig",
        "timestamp": 1780246929
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Alternatively, if you just want something simple to familiarize yourself with the contribution process, here's some point-set topology instances that are still missing from mathlib:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">PathConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">PathConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PathConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--fails</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LocPathConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LocPathConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LocPathConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--fails</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LocallyConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LocallyConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LocallyConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--fails</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PathConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PathConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--fails</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PathConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LocPathConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">LocPathConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--fails</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LocallyConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">LocallyConnectedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--fails</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I think topology is generally a nice entry point for getting started with mathlib, since there are a lot fewer moving parts than in e.g. differential geometry, and hence a lot less things that can go wrong. Probably any number of these could be a good first contribution, ideally together with some corresponding lemmas about <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=connectedComponent#doc\">docs#connectedComponent</a> / <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=connectedComponentIn#doc\">docs#connectedComponentIn</a> / <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=pathComponent#doc\">docs#pathComponent</a> / <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=pathComponentIn#doc\">docs#pathComponentIn</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsPathConnected#doc\">docs#IsPathConnected</a> in product spaces too</p>",
        "id": 599010602,
        "sender_full_name": "Ben Eltschig",
        "timestamp": 1780247730
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"635099\">@Gaëtan Serré</span>  and <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"646363\">@Ben Eltschig</span>  thank you so much for the warm welcome -- will be thoughtful about your responses and think about a good path forward. I don't want to go rambo and start creating pull requests to Mathlib without the community's blessing. Thank you both for the pointers, examples, and advice.</p>",
        "id": 599063821,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Korbonits",
        "timestamp": 1780288700
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>OK, I did a think <span aria-label=\"eyes\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f440\" role=\"img\" title=\"eyes\">:eyes:</span>   <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40092\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40092</a> — \"feat(Topology/Connected): path-connectedness of products and pi types\"</p>\n<p>LMK what you think -- I directly followed your advice on missing point set topology examples. Makes me remember Munkres (would be interesting to go through that and see what is formalized in that book alone, no?).</p>",
        "id": 599065369,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Korbonits",
        "timestamp": 1780289780
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Welcome! I have a concrete, self-contained requirement around the exponential map and flows you mentioned. Several caveats:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>I have not really introduced myself even though I have been using Lean / Mathlib for 18+ months.</li>\n<li>I have not contributed to Mathlib although I have a PR on the existence of Riemannian metrics pending: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/33714\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/33714</a>.</li>\n<li>Not sure that this is a first theorem to attempt but I may as well state it.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>I think Zulip's restrictions on message size means I will have to split up what I have to say.</p>\n<p><strong>The goal.</strong> Proving the Lie group exponential map is smooth. For a Lie group <code>G</code> modelled on a normed space <code>EG</code>, Lie algebra <code>g = T_e G</code>, the left-invariant vector field <code>X_v</code> (<code>v ∈ g</code>) has an integral curve <code>γ_v</code> through the identity, and <code>exp(v) := γ_v(1)</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">contMDiff_expLie</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">T2Space</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CompleteSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EG</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BoundarylessManifold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ContMDiff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝓘</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EG</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">minSmoothness</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expLie</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(C² out, since a C³ Lie group gives a C² exponential. Ref: Meinrenken, <em>Lie Groups and Lie Algebras</em>, §3–4.)<br>\n<strong>The dependency chain:</strong></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">contMDiff_expLie</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">needs</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Lee</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">9.12</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SMOOTH</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">version</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">smooth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">joint</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">flow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">needs</span>\n<span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SMOOTH</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">local</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">flow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ODE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">smooth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dependence</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">initial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">condition</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"bp\">—</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">which</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">does</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NOT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">yet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Mathlib <em>has</em> the <strong>continuous</strong> local-flow result (Winston Yin's). Using it, I've proved Lee 9.12 at the <strong>continuous</strong> level only. The single gap between continuous and smooth is the regularity of that one ODE input. Details in the next message.</p>",
        "id": 599347445,
        "sender_full_name": "Dominic Steinitz",
        "timestamp": 1780390389
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><strong>(1) Winston's result — continuous local flow</strong> (<a href=\"https://github.com/winstonyin/mathlib4/blob/e4a394e66bb158c6271f5e8dd130c7726a72bcd6/Mathlib/Geometry/Manifold/IntegralCurve/ExistUnique.lean#L107\"><code>ExistUnique.lean</code> L107</a>):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- Existence of local flows for a C¹ vector field at interior points of a C¹ manifold. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exists_mem_nhds_isMIntegralCurveOn_Ioo_of_contMDiffAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CompleteSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContMDiffAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I.tangent</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TangentBundle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x₀</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I.IsInteriorPoint</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x₀</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝓝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x₀</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t₀</span><span class=\"o\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">IsMIntegralCurveOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">⟩)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Ioo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×ˢ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ioo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(Name's a bit misleading: <code>contMDiffAt</code> is the <em>input</em> hypothesis; the <em>output</em> joint flow is only <code>ContinuousOn</code>.)<br>\n<strong>(2) My continuous Lee 9.12</strong> (<a href=\"https://github.com/idontgetoutmuch/mathlib4/blob/bcf4ceec3dc9f130302404aba69701544d39a6a0/Mathlib/Geometry/Manifold/Algebra/MaximalFlow.lean\"><code>MaximalFlow.lean</code></a>). Core: <code>W_lee_eq_flowSet_lee : W_lee V hV = flowSet V</code> — Lee's Fundamental Theorem on Flows (flow domain open, maximal flow defined on it) — giving joint continuity of <code>(t,x) ↦ maximalFlowAt' V x t</code> on <code>flowSet V</code>.</p>\n<p>Key structural point: Winston's lemma is used in <em>exactly</em> the base case (<code>zero_mem_flowDomain</code>, <code>mem_W_lee_zero_lee</code>), and the output regularity equals the regularity of the <code>γ</code> it hands us. Everything downstream (<code>flowDomain_extend</code>, the piecewise gluing lemmas, the <code>sInf</code> argument) only <em>propagates</em> that regularity via uniqueness of integral curves. Proved except one <code>sorry</code>: <code>W_lee_neg_time</code> (the τ ≤ 0 branch), the time-reversed (<code>t ↦ -t</code>) copy of the proven τ &gt; 0 argument.</p>\n<p>⇒ <strong>If Winston's lemma's output were <code>ContMDiff</code> instead of <code>ContinuousOn</code>, the base case upgrades and the whole file re-runs verbatim with <code>ContMDiff</code> for <code>ContinuousOn</code></strong> — turning the smooth Lee 9.12, and hence <code>contMDiff_expLie</code>, into theorems. The whole smoothness gap is concentrated in that one ODE input.</p>",
        "id": 599348009,
        "sender_full_name": "Dominic Steinitz",
        "timestamp": 1780390568
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><strong>(3) What's needed — smooth local flow, as a proof_wanted.</strong> The Cⁿ upgrade of Winston's lemma, same statement with <code>ContinuousOn</code> → <code>ContMDiff</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">proof_wanted</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exists_mem_nhds_isMIntegralCurveOn_Ioo_of_contMDiffAt_smooth</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CompleteSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContMDiffAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I.tangent</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TangentBundle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x₀</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I.IsInteriorPoint</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x₀</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝓝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x₀</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t₀</span><span class=\"o\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">IsMIntegralCurveOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">⟩)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Ioo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">ContMDiff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">𝓘</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">⟩)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Banach-space ingredient that should feed this: <code>SmoothFlow.exists_localFlow</code> (Winston's PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/34288\">#34288</a>) gives <code>ContDiffAt</code>of the curve-<em>valued</em> map in the initial condition — but joint <code>(t,x)</code> smoothness still needs the time-direction + evaluation step; not a free corollary.<br>\n<strong>Also worth helping along — Winston's PRs</strong> (general benefit to diff geom, not all strictly on the critical path):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>#34288</strong> \"Integral curve is smooth in initial condition\" (Analysis/ODE — <em>not</em> t-differential-geometry, so won't show on a t-differential-geometry queueboard filter). The Banach ingredient for (3). Open; review by @j-loreaux in progress.</li>\n<li><strong>#26394</strong> \"existence of local flows on manifolds\" — failing CI; unblocked.</li>\n<li><strong>#26395</strong> \"C¹ vector fields on compact manifolds define global flows\" — WIP, blocked-by-other-PR, merge-conflict.</li>\n<li><strong>#9341</strong> \"Naturality of integral curves\" — merge-conflict, awaiting-author.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I hope that makes sense. I should say the diff geom bit of Mathlib takes a bit of getting used to. It's taken me a year.</p>\n<p>Also you can look here for what's going on: <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/queueboard/on_the_queue.html?pr_type=feat&amp;pr_type=other&amp;topic_label=t-differential-geometry&amp;sort=author-asc\">https://leanprover-community.github.io/queueboard/on_the_queue.html?pr_type=feat&amp;pr_type=other&amp;topic_label=t-differential-geometry&amp;sort=author-asc</a></p>\n<p>It's a shame there is not a diff geom progress meeting like the one for Brownian motion.</p>",
        "id": 599349371,
        "sender_full_name": "Dominic Steinitz",
        "timestamp": 1780390894
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"754300\">Dominic Steinitz</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Alex.20Korbonits.2C.20ML.20scientist.20wanting.20to.20learn.20lean/near/599347445\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think Zulip's restrictions on message size means I will have to split up what I have to say.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Hello! Can you clarify whether this is output from an LLM?</p>",
        "id": 599354770,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1780392577
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>No</p>",
        "id": 599356036,
